# Mission Control (cursor-workspace)

When `QUOTA_TRACKER_URL` is set, push status before/after meaningful phases:
exploring, coding, testing, blocked, pr-ready, done.

```bash
python3 scripts/agent_status.py push \
  --phase "<phase>" \
  --summary "<one short sentence>" \
  --status live \
  --test-status unknown|running|green|failed
```

Blocked / PR ready:

```bash
python3 scripts/agent_status.py push --phase blocked --attention --attention-reason "Need env var"
python3 scripts/agent_status.py push --phase pr-ready --attention --pr-url "https://github.com/..."
```

Requires env: `QUOTA_TRACKER_URL`, `QUOTA_TRACKER_TOKEN`, `QUOTA_TRACKER_ID` (default `cursor-workspace`).

Rules:
- Never send secrets, tokens, API keys, private prompts, or file contents in summary/metrics.
- `attention=true` only when blocked, tests fail, PR ready, or user action needed.
- If POST fails, continue the task — do not loop retries.
- If `QUOTA_TRACKER_URL` is unset, skip silently.
